OK.  So, I manage to get nethack installed on a PC where I work.  My job cur-
rently is not related to computing, but I manage to snag some time on some-
one else's machine now and then to merrily hack away.  I'm not that great, 
but I'm getting better, learning more and more, etc.  It's an interesting 
something to do on long, boring nights.

So I play a game last week, one of my best, and when it's over, find that, 
not only have I not made the scoreboard, but the entire top ten list has 
been consumed by this other guy's character!  And his scores beat mine by a 
MILE!  All well and good, I say to myself, after the initial shock.  I should
talk to this guy, looks like he's a pretty damn good nethack player.

Then I notice:  the bastard is pulling the old save-rename-recover trick!  By
the opinions of myself and at least a few others here, that's out and out 
cheating!  So, the ethical dilemma I pose to you is such:

1) Do I recognize that he, as a free and thinking being, has a right to his 
own ethical belief system and leave it alone? or

2) Do I recognize that he's a jerk and erase all his save positions? or

3) Do I recognize that I'm a REALLY nasty individual and erase all his save 
positions except for the last one, enter the game on the last save position,
drink the potion of blindness he's carrying, drop all of his stuff, and 
level teleport away, inscribing "The Gods are displeased, arrogant Mortal!"
in the dust at his feet?  :)

Note:  I'll probably go for option 1, just curious what it takes to start a 
flamewar on r.g.h.  *grin*

